# Learning-oriented comments

This project is the **Viscous Memory** hand-fluid piece (p5 + MediaPipe). When you add or change code in the core files (`app.tsx`, `sketch.tsx`, `fluid-content-layer.tsx`, input broker, store, config):

1. **Add a short comment** that explains *what* the code does and *why* it is done that way (e.g. why this hook, why this order, why this value).
2. Prefer comments above a block or next to a non-obvious line; avoid commenting every line.
3. Use **English** for these comments so they stay consistent with `docs/learning/hand-fluid-mediapipe-guide.md`.

Example:

```ts
// Run camera tilt in useFrame so it stays in sync with the 3D render loop; we keep the mouse listener in useEffect to avoid re-attaching every frame.
useFrame(({ camera }) => { ... });
```

```ts
// Low alpha (28) clears the canvas only partially each frame, so previous positions remain visible and form the trail.
p.background(7, 11, 20, 28);
```
